 "answer_text": "Found 1 gene record for Huntington disease: huntingtin [13]. \n\nA derived record for NCBIGene:3064 was also retrieved [1]. \n\nGenetic Testing Principles\n\nA recent review covers the epidemiology, genetic basis, pathogenesis, presentation, and clinical management of Huntington disease, and explicitly explains the principles of genetic testing [2]. \n\nClinical Features\n\nMedGen lists these clinical features: Chorea [3], Depression [4], Gliosis [5], Rigidity [6], Seizure [7], Hyperreflexia [8], Bradykinesia [9], Personality changes [10], Abnormality of eye movement [11] and Dementia [12]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene NCBIGene:3064, name: huntingtin [13]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Huntington disease [14]. Pubmed title: Huntington disease [21]. Pubmed title: Huntington disease [23]. Pubmed title: Huntington disease: When does it begin [25]. Pubmed title: What Is Huntington Disease [27]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Huntington disease [15]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Huntington disease\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Chorea [3]. Medgen clinical_features: Depression [4]. Medgen clinical_features: Gliosis [5]. Medgen clinical_features: Rigidity [6]. Medgen clinical_features: Seizure [7]. Medgen clinical_features: Hyperreflexia [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Bradykinesia [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Personality changes [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Abnormality of eye movement [11]. Medgen clinical_features: Dementia [12]. Medgen clinical_features: Cerebellar atrophy [16]. Medgen clinical_features: Gait ataxia [17]. Medgen clinical_features: Neuronal loss in central nervous system [18]. \n\nLiterature entity records found\n\nLiterature entity name: Huntington Disease [19]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: Prospective Huntington At Risk Observational Study [20]. Clinical trial name: Family Health After Predictive Huntington Disease (HD) Testing [22]. Clinical trial name: Bioavailability of Ubiquinol in Huntington Disease [24]. Clinical trial name: Study of Huntington Patients in Connection With European Huntington's Disease Network (EHDN) [26]. Clinical trial name: Resveratrol and Huntington Disease [28]. "
